      "constraints": "approved",
      "rationale": [
        "Reviewed deferred bootstrap order, prewarm variants and worker affinity. The graph manager is constructed within model_runner; no independent capture worker starts until an inference warmup or composite request.",
        "prepare_startup_assets now reads the manager-owned profile directory. Consumers retain manifest validation; observations cannot overwrite frozen inputs.",
        "Weight/compile overlap remains internal to the joined load action. compile_already_ready preserves its readiness output without repeating compilation. KV allocation and graph precapture remain behind real compile and memory readiness.",
        "Precapture delegates to one executor and registry. Runtime warmup precedes background capture; partial graphs stay private. GraphAdapter preserves cost guards, KV-safe fallbacks and unified sampling. Capture drains before model rebind.",
        "Structured-output and scheduler state producers, final readiness and prepared asset release are unchanged. Reviewed within the existing single-GPU adapter scope."
      ]
    },
